comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-10T22:05:05.431Z",pi-agent,"Delivered: promotion.ts is a pure fail-closed statistically bounded promotion gate (Hoeffding inequality over bounded-reward sample evidence). It enforces that a candidate is promoted ONLY when its held-out lower confidence bound exceeds the incumbent's upper bound by the effect threshold, with confidence 1-alpha over at least minSamples episodes, and the held-out set is isolated from training (contamination verdict null). Default is NO. Integrated into bandit.ts: the recursive loop now draws seeded held-out evaluation episodes and gates each promotion through decidePromotion, recording every refusal reason on the generation receipt (refusalReason) so the generations array is the auditable lineage. Adversarial tests in test/promotion.test.ts (19 tests) and test/bandit.test.ts (4 new gate tests) cover: no evidence -> refused; wrong generation -> refused; contaminated held-out -> refused; single lucky sample below minSamples -> refused; genuine statistically sound improvement -> promoted; regression -> refused with reason; minimize direction; transitive invalidation via existing buildLineageAncestry; determinism. Revert-check: neutering decidePromotion to always-promote turns 14 promotion tests RED (5 pass: pure parse/bound helpers + deterministic + transitive invalidation, which do not depend on the refusal behaviour). Coverage 100/100/100/100, docstrings 100%, no any, no inline await import, erasable TS only."
